__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
# `full` writes these two at the repository root on its way to publishing the README badges --
# `coverage json -o coverage.json`, then docs/badges/publish_badges.py into badges/. Neither is
# ever committed: the whole point of the change away from committed SVGs is that a badge with no
# run behind it should go visibly stale rather than sit in the repository looking current.
coverage.json
/badges/
docs/_build/
.ruff_cache/
# *.sql
# *.db
# n2.html
# coloring_files/
# run_outputs/
# IPOPT.out
# SLSQP.out

# OpenMDAO litter, but ONLY where it lands by accident. A pattern with no leading slash matches at
# every depth, so a bare `reports/` and `*_out/` also swallowed run_outputs/<case>_<stamp>_out/ and
# the reports/ inside each one -- which is the very output that is meant to be committed. Anchored
# to the repository root, these still catch a stray run started from the wrong directory.
/reports/
/*_out/

# pyXDSM build output. The .tex, .tikz and .png are committed -- the PNG is what GitHub and the
# docs display, so it has to be in the repository. The PDF and the LaTeX litter are not: the PDF
# is regenerable from the .tex in one command and is only wanted for print.
docs/xdsm/*.pdf
docs/xdsm/*.aux
docs/xdsm/*.log
docs/xdsm/*.out
